% c086: Bsn 1 breathes at 116 with Hn 4, which plays the same tenor line and has breathed there since c046 (20 bars of f-ff from 101 otherwise; Sebesky PDF 24: a slur is played in one breath).
% c189: 117 tenor countermelody (Bsn 1, Hn 3, Hn 4, Vc) G3 then E4 on beat 3 (was E4 for the bar): the seventh A3 of B7 at 116 now resolves down by step in its own voice (A-S PDF 399-400, 375), and the phrase restarts with the countermelody's opening shape G-E (105-106).
% c358: 105/305 "espress." on Bsn 1 and Hn 3(-4), which double the cellos' countermelody (marked espress.) at the same ff (Sebesky Ex. 281, PDF 214-215). No accent or dynamic added (soft-brass rule).
sCBsnOne = { g2.(^\markup \italic "espress." | b2 e'4~ | e'2 b4 | a2 fis4 | g2.) | a2( c'4~ | c'4 b4 a4 | g2.) | c'2.( | b2. | a2 c'4 | b2 a4) \breathe | g2( e'4~ | e'2 g4 | a2 fis4 | g4) r4 r4 | R2.*4 | a2(\p\< e4~ | e4 fis2) | g2( a4~ | a4 b2) | b2.~\f | b2. | e2. | e4-. r4 r4 | e2.--(\p | e2.-- | e2.--\> | e2.--)\! | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | }
% c014: 105-120 the sustained bass goes to Bsn 2 and the bass trombone plays the accented downbeats with the tuba (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 101, 104); Tpt 2 E4 (not D sharp) in the tonic bar 109
% c362 (A&S Unit 5, PDF 83): Bsn 2 stops on beat 3 of 109 and 117 (the tune's E there leaps E-A, E-G with the bass): no octaves with the tune, as at 112 (c066)
sCBsnTwo = { e,2. | e,2. | e,2. | b,2. | e,2 r4 | a,2. | b,2. | e,2 r4 | a,2. | gis,2. | a,2. | b,2. | e,2 r4 | g,2. | b,2. | e,4 r4 r4 | e,2\subP e4~ | e4 g,2 | b,2 a,4~ | a,4 g,2 | a,2\p\< c4~ | c4 b,2 | e2 fis4~ | fis4 g2 | b,2.~\f | b,2. | e,2. | e,4-. r4 r4 | R2.*8 | }  % c066: breath for Bsn 2 at the theme's phrase end (Vln I rests on beats 2-3 here): 24 bars of ff sustained bass otherwise (Adler PDF 230, 292)
% c148: 105-120 (and 305-320 in dC) Cb and Cbsn tenuto, not accent, on every tutti downbeat, as the tuba, bass trombone and timpani (c124, c146): the bar line already carries the metrical accent in one-to-the-bar 3/4, and 16 equal accents flatten the four-bar hypermeasure (Aldwell-Schachter Unit 3 PDF 50, 53); Dvorak 9/iii marks accents only where they go against the metre.
sCCbsn = { e,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | b,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | a,,4-- r4 r4 | b,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | a,,4-- r4 r4 | gis,,4-- r4 r4 | a,,4-- r4 r4 | b,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | g,,4-- r4 r4 | b,,4-- r4 r4 | e,,4-- r4 r4 | R2.*4 | a,,2(\p\< c,4~ | c,4 b,,2) | e,2( fis,4~ | fis,4 g,2) | b,,2.~\f | b,,2. | e,,2. | e,,4-. r4 r4 | R2.*8 | }
% c124: 105-120 the brass downbeat crotchets tenuto instead of accented (horns ff, low brass f unchanged): Dan's listening rule (BRIEF: brass weight, not bite);
%   Adler II PDF 147-148 (d'Indy: trombones held under the tutti so they do not dominate), PDF 154 (Smetana: the brass give the fast tutti roundness, not edge).
% c165: Hn 1-4 do not restate ff at 105: the ff reached at 104 stands (one dynamic per change, MOLA PDF 8 and Ex. 3)
% c189: 113 beat 3 Hn 1 A4 (was C5): C5-B4 against the passing F sharp 4-E4 of CA, Cl 2 and Vln II made a diminished fifth move to a perfect fifth by similar motion between upper voices (A-S PDF 375, Ex. 22-3c: avoid); A4 is a chord tone of iv and moves to B4 in contrary motion.
% c202: 110 Hn 1 beat 3 A4 (was C5): C5-B4 against the tune's G-F# into 111 made the IV8-7-V parallel fifths of Aldwell-Schachter Ex. 12-21 (PDF 190) between Hn 1 and the melody; A4 steps to B4 as at 113/313 (c189)
% c272: 110 Hn 1 rests on beat 3 (was A4, c202): A4-B4 moved in octaves with the bass A-B into 111 (Aldwell-Schachter PDF 83, Ex. 5-18); C5 on the downbeat and c202's removal of the fifths stay
sCHnOne = { b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 r4 | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | c''4-- r4 r4 | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | c''4-- r4 a'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | c''4-- r4 c''4-. | fis'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 r4 | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | b'4-- r4 b'4-. | R2.*20 | }  % c011: no E on beat 3 of 106/118 (310/322) under the chromatic tail F sharp-F-E (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 54)  % c046: Hn 1 rests from 121 after 16 bars at E5 ff; Hn 3 takes the sustained line 121-132 (Adler PDF 292, 303: periodic rests in the high register) % c066: Hn 1 on B4/C5 (written F#5/G5), not E5 (written B5, a semitone under the professional ceiling C6 in Adler App. A, adler2 PDF 305); Hn 3 takes the middle G4/A4/F#4 (Adler PDF 303-304: III between I and II); Hn 3 beat 1 only at 106/118 (G against the tail F#-F)
sCHnTwo = { e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 r4 | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | dis'4-- r4 dis'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | dis'4-- r4 dis'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | dis'4-- r4 dis'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | e'4-- r4 r4 | fis'4-- r4 dis'4-. | e'4-- r4 e'4-. | g'2.--(\subP | g'2.-- | fis'2.--~ | fis'4 g'2--) | e'2.(\< | e'4 dis'2 | e'2 b4~ | b4 e'2) | g'2.--(\mf | fis'2.--~ | fis'4-\sysLabel "2." e'2--) | e'4-. r4 r4 | R2.*8 | }  % c046: Hn 2 takes the E4 crotchets and Hn 3 the B4 (Adler PDF 303: I and III high, II and IV low)  % c325: \sysLabel "2." at 131 (page 6 starts with Hn 2 alone on the Hn 1·2 staff; Adler II PDF 295)
% c166: 121-128 the held B3/C4 under the second idea moves from Hn 3 to Hn 4 (pitches, slurs, dynamics unchanged; hidden mf ends the hairpin, c138), so Hn 3 rests
%   eight bars after 20 bars of p<ff and ff tenor line (101-120) before its f B4 at 129 (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 37, 44: give wind and brass players a little rest from time to time;
%   the low held notes suit the even horn). Hn 4 rests from 129. The reprise already rests Hn 3 at 281-284 (c157).
% c358: 105/305 "espress." on Bsn 1 and Hn 3(-4), which double the cellos' countermelody (marked espress.) at the same ff (Sebesky Ex. 281, PDF 214-215). No accent or dynamic added (soft-brass rule).
sCHnFour = { g2.(-\tag #'part ^\markup \italic "espress." | b2 e'4~ | e'2 b4 | a2 fis4 | g2.) | a2( c'4~ | c'4 b4 a4 | g2.) | c'2.( | b2. | a2 c'4 | b2 a4) \once \override BreathingSign.direction = #DOWN \breathe | g2( e'4~ | e'2 g4 | a2 fis4 | g4) r4 r4 | b2.--(\subP | b2.-- | b2.-- | b2.--) | c'2.--(\< | c'2.-- | b2.-- | b2.--\mf) | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | }  % c046: the 16-bar forte legato is split at 116/117 (316/317) for a breath (Adler PDF 292, 309: a slur is one breath)
% c025: Hn 3 and Hn 4 exchanged at 105-120/305-320: the low countermelody (G3-E4) was in Hn 3, the upper voice of the shared staff, under Hn 4's E4 crotchets, so the voices crossed in every bar (Gould, Behind Bars PDF 41, 50-51)
% c088: 121-132 (and 277-288 in dA) Hn 2 and Hn 3 sustained chords under phrase slurs with tenuto on repeated notes (Adler I PDF 309).
% c097: 105-120 Hn 3 joins Hn 4 in unison on the tenor countermelody (with Vc and Bsn 1); Hn 1-2 keep the crotchet chords on beats 1 and 3
%   (Adler II PDF 44: two horns in unison equal one trumpet or trombone; one horn under three ff horns, trumpets and four low brass is covered).
% c109: 121-128 Hn 3 B3/C4 (was B4/C5): the held horn sat at the unison on the first note of each phrase of the second idea's lower octave (Vln II B4 at 121, Vln II and Ob 1 C5 at 125) and inside its compass (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 54: a melody in the middle register needs relief; PDF 78; c084 at 45); B3 fills the gap between the bass and the violas. 129-132 unchanged.
% c358: 105/305 "espress." on Bsn 1 and Hn 3(-4), which double the cellos' countermelody (marked espress.) at the same ff (Sebesky Ex. 281, PDF 214-215). No accent or dynamic added (soft-brass rule).
sCHnThree = { g2.(^\markup \italic "espress." | b2 e'4~ | e'2 b4 | a2 fis4 | g2.) | a2( c'4~ | c'4-\sysLabel "a2" b4 a4 | g2.) | c'2.( | b2. | a2 c'4 | b2 a4) \breathe | g2( e'4~ | e'2 g4 | a2 fis4 | g4) r4 r4 | R2.*8 | b'2.--(\mf | a'2.--~ | a'4-\sysLabel "3." g'2--) | g'4-. r4 r4 | R2.*8 | }  % c011: no E on beat 3 of 106/118 (310/322) under the chromatic tail F sharp-F-E (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 54)  % c325: \sysLabel "a2" at 111 (page 5 starts with Hn 3·4 in unison, last labelled at 105) and "3." at 131 (page 6, Hn 3 alone) (Adler II PDF 295: all instruments clearly marked in all systems)
