% c045: 121 (H) the second idea's accompaniment marked f in Cl 1-2, Bn 1-2, Cbn, Vla, Vc, Cb with the melody: these parts still read ff from 104-105,
%   louder than the f melody (MOLA PDF 8: proofread the vertical line; as at 45, where every part is marked f).
% c067: 113-120 Vln II takes theme A an octave lower (with Cl 2 and the cor anglais) for the tutti's second half; 105-112 stay in unison
%   (Sebesky PDF 140 rule 6: a strong concerted string melody is reinforced an octave lower; PDF 151, Ex. 202: the octave below is added as the
%   passage builds; PDF 168: strings are the weakest element in a mixed tutti). The reprise (305-320) keeps its octaves from the start (c029).
% c067: 121-124 Bsn 1 rests (it doubled Vc and Bsn 2 an octave up under the sub. p); it enters at 125 with Fl 1 and Ob 1 on its own line
%   (A-E-D sharp, the third of V at 126). Sebesky PDF 140 rule 7 and PDF 145-146: the bass doubled for its own sake "grounds" a soft texture and clouds the bass line.
% c074: 121-124 the contrabassoon rests and enters p< at 125 with the crescendo: the sub. p bass was in four instruments (Vc, Bsn 2, Cb, Cbn);
%   Adler I PDF 130 (the bass is dropped when a lighter string texture is wanted and returns at the cadence), PDF 154 (diminuendo and lightness by scoring), PDF 137 (crescendo by adding octaves).
% c112: 110-111 tenor (Hn 3, Hn 4, Bsn 1, Vc) C4 tied over the bar as a 9-8 over V: removes the 5ths with the tune's G-F# (IV8-7-V, A-S Ex. 12-21, PDF 190). 108 violas B3 (no 5ths with the bass E-B-E). 124 Hn 2/Vla F#4-G4 (no 5ths with the tune's C#6-B5).
% c132: 127 Bsn 1 G3 (was E3): at 126-127 the d5 F sharp 3-C4 (Bsn 1 against Cl 2, violas and Hn 3 on the ♭9 C4) resolves inward to the 3rd G3-B3
%   instead of moving in similar motion to the P5 E3-B3 (Aldwell-Schachter PDF 375, Ex. 22-3a/c). c082's complete V♭9 and single leading tone are kept.
% c174: 129 Hn 2 and Hn 3 mf, a level under the f tune, whose lower octave (Ob 1, Vln II) they double at B4 and F sharp 4 (Casanelles PDF 271-272, 287, 289; as c084 at 45)
% c205: 105 (and 305 in dC.ily) Ob 2's two crotchet rests at one height (staff-position -6, below Ob 1's B4 quavers); the beat-3 rest was a space higher than the beat-2 rest, a staggered pair (Gould, Behind Bars PDF 49-51: rests move whole spaces, lower-part rests below the centre and at the level of the surrounding pitches). Score only (\tag #'score): the Ob 2 part keeps centred rests (PDF 49).
% c392 (A&S PDF 123, 128: V4/3 as a passing chord between i and i6, its 7th rising when it moves in 10ths with the bass; Unit 17 PDF 269: 10-10 over 8-8; Unit 5 PDF 83):
%   127-128 Bsn 1 G3-A3-B3 in tenths over the bass E2-F#2-G2 (was G3-F#3-G3: octaves G-F# with Cl 1 at 127 and F#-G with the bass at 127-128); 127 beat 3 is now V4/3, not a bare V6/4.
